FREQP
FREQP.FT	FREQ DATA PRINTOUT
		MH-ICD,MN.		07/31/75.


FREQP- PRINTOUT DATA COLLECTED USING PROGRAM "FREQ" WITH BLOCK
AVERAGES OF FREQUENCY & INTENSITY LISTING  AND/OR  INDIVIDUAL
TIME SEGMENTS PRINTED. THE BLOCK AVERAGES COLUMNS MEAN:


#	BLOCK NUMBER BEING AVERAGED.

TIME	REAL TIME IN MINUTES.SECONDS AT END OF BLOCK. WHEN THE
	VOLTAGE FOR 80 DB IS ENTERED ON THE TELETYPE, THIS TIME IS
	RESET TO ZERO.

FREQB	THE AVERAGE FREQUENCY IN HERTZ OF THE BLOCK. FREQUENCIES
	BELOW 70 HERTZ AND ABOVE 450 HERTZ ARE NOT AVERAGED.

VOLTS	AVERAGE VOLTAGE OF SOUND SEGMENTS.

DB	DB SPL CCMPAIRED TO 80 DB CALIBRATION TONE.

SAMPL	NUMBER OF VOLTAGE POINTS USED IN EACH SOUND SEGMENT.

COUNT	NUMBER OF VOLTAGE POINTS USED IN AVERAGE OF THE FREQUENCY
	THIS BLOCK. RANGES FROM 0 TO 64 POINTS.


THE INDIVIDUAL SOUND TIME SEGMENTS ARE LISTED IN COLUMNS OF 64
PER BLOCK, WITH 8 BLOCKS ON A PAGE. THE WIDE 128 CHARACTER PAPER
SHOULD BE LOADED IN THE PRINTER. THE FIRST NUMBER IN THE HEADING
LINE IS THE BLOCK NUMBER OF THE FIRST COLUMN. THE HEADER MEANS:

F	FREQUENCY IN HERTZ.

#S	NUMBER OF SAMPLE VOLTAGES TAKEN.

VOLT	VOLTAGE OF SOUND SEGMENT. THIS IS THE SUM OF ALL THE
	SAMPLE VOLTAGES.
FREQP
	FREQP OPTIONS AND INPUTS.
	- - - - - - - - - - - - -

1. HLT	AC=0077. FIRST PAUSE, SET THE STARTING BLOCK NUMBER TO
	BEGIN PRINTING IN THE RIGHT SWITCHES.
   RS=	FIRST BLOCK OF DATA TO PRINT.
  CONT

2. HLT	AC=0007. SET RIGHT SWITCHES TO LAST BLOCK TO PRINT ON THE
	DATA TAPE. THE OTHER SENSE SWITCH OPTIONS ARE NOW SET AND
	SHOULD REMAIN SET UNTIL PRINTOUT IS COMPLETE.

   RS=	LAST BLOCK OF DATA TO PRINT.

   SW0	ON	PRINT INDIVIDUAL TIME SOUND SEGMENTS.

   SW4	ON	PRINTOUT SENT TO LINE PRINTER. BE SURE TO USE
		128 COLUMN PAPER.
	OFF	PRINTOUT SENT TO FILE SYS:SCR.DA FOR LATER PRINTOUT
		OR SPOT CHECKING USING SCROLL.

   SW5	ON	SKIP PRINTING BLOCK AVERAGES OF SOUND FREQUENCIES.
	OFF	PRINT BLOCK AVERAGES.

3.	FREQP WILL PRINTOUT ON THE TELETYPE ASKING FOR THE 80 DB
	VOLTAGE. LOOK UNDER COLUMN LABELED "VOLT". ENTER "0" IF VOLTAGE
	IS UNSATISFACTORY. FREQP WILL ASK AGAIN UNTIL IT IS SATISFACTORY.

4. FREQP RETURNS TO THE OS/12S MONITOR WHEN FINISHED.


****
SEE:	FREQ.WU FOR SOUND DATA COLLECTION INFORMATION.
